  "note": "Q1133288/way131451819 identifies the archaeological site. Seven pinned standard PMTiles components control the surviving podium, shelter, four concrete cores and short southern foundation trace. The broad historic site boundary is context, not a solid building to extrude. The curved shelter/recess and ordinary northwest frontal picture establish the altar front toward northwest, with an internal architectural rotation of about 124 degrees. Raw +X remains east and +Z south at runtime heading 0. Neighboring Arch of Augustus components east of the temple are explicitly excluded. The retained standard Mapzen grid is unchanged. Each surviving core has a buried retaining foundation and a locally seated datum; the altar floor and modern canopy remain near the northwest local grade. Ground and water stay native with no cutout. Archaeological excavation floors and current damage are not surveyed. Preview uses the host terrain sample at the authored base; ground slope, facade azimuth and final site fit remain review items."
